# macOS app build gate

Do not tell the user your changes are done, complete, or ready until the macOS app build has finished successfully in this session.

## When this applies

- Any change that touches the app bundle, packaging, client, server, or dependencies that feed `Referee.app`
- When the user asks for a feature, fix, or refactor in this repo unless they explicitly scope work to non-macOS targets only

## Required verification (macOS)

From the repository root:

```bash
./build-app.sh
```

The build must exit 0 and print `Built: .../build/macos/Referee.app`.

## If the build fails

- Fix the failure (compile errors, missing assets, packaging scripts, etc.) and re-run `./build-app.sh` until it passes
- Report build failures and fixes in your summary; do not skip the gate because the change "looks small"

## Non-macOS environments

If you cannot run on macOS (e.g. Linux-only sandbox), say so clearly, run whatever subset is possible (e.g. `client` and `server` builds), and do **not** claim the macOS app is verified until `./build-app.sh` has been run successfully on macOS.

## Completion wording

- OK: "Build passed (`./build-app.sh` → `build/macos/Referee.app`)."
- Not OK: "Should work" / "Ready to merge" without a successful `./build-app.sh` on macOS when this gate applies
